    "narrative": "Our offensive engine for June 12th is anchored by **Taylor Ward** (67.27) and **Luis Arraez** (67.31), both of whom benefit significantly from favorable matchups. **Taylor Ward** leads our daily efficiency scores thanks to a premium park factor (+16%) and a high-leverage leadoff spot, capitalizing on his matchup against Canning. Meanwhile, **Luis Arraez** and **Matt Chapman** (66.76) should thrive against Javier Assad; while the park factor in Chicago slightly dampens the upside, the combination of a middling 4.63 xERA starter and elevated batting order positions gives both an elite floor. **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.52) remains a high-value play as a scarcity specialist; he effectively neutralized the threat of Lodolo by securing a +4% platoon boost and solid park alignment, making him a critical component of our quest for stolen bases.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card involved keeping **Bryson Stott** (48.48) on the bench. While he offers a strong platoon advantage (+13%) against Misiorowski, his efficiency was suppressed by the opposing pitcher\u2019s elite xERA (2.79), which significantly penalized his baseline projection. Ultimately, we prioritized the higher raw offensive outputs of **Gavin Sheets** (64.98), who enjoys an advantageous matchup in a hitter-friendly park, and **Jung Hoo Lee** (63.63), whose dynamic platoon edge against Assad keeps him firmly in the OF2 slot. We are proceeding with caution regarding the pending lineups for **Jonathan Aranda**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Drew Gilbert**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Matt Chapman**; should any of these players be moved down the order, their efficiency scores will require immediate re-evaluation against the depth currently idling on our bench. With **Yainer Diaz** and **Cal Raleigh** still sidelined, maintaining high daily efficiency from the active roster remains the priority to navigate our game cap constraints.",
